WEBVTT

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.510
<i>My every nerve is</i>

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.510
<i>connected through my fingertips</i>

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.350
<i>with the game, the lever,</i>

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.620
<i>the buttons, and the screen.</i>

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.420
<i>Ono,</i>

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.190
<i>do you remember the first time
we battled at the arcade?</i>

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.530
<i>The day you fought...</i>

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.360
<i>Haruo of the Mighty Fingers!</i>

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:39.970
<i>No more turtling Guile</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.570
<i>or cowardly tactics.
This is the right way to fight with Guile.</i>

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.740
<i>Jump, and you'll get a Somersault Kick.</i>

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:47.780
<i>A Lift Upper also awaits.</i>

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.710
<i>They used to say
I didn't fight like a man.</i>

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.820
<i>But with</i> Super Street Fighter II Turbo,

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.790
<i>this is the way to fight with Guile!</i>

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.590
<i>I'll wait and wait and wait forever.</i>

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.820
<i>This wall of steel will never fall!</i>

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.190
This is brutal!

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.930
<i>Watch his jumps carefully.</i>

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.660
<i>Don't miss a single frame!</i>

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.100
<i>Don't let him get close!</i>

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.530
<i>This steel wall,</i>

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.270
<i>just try to knock it down if you dare!</i>

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.240
<i>Just you try to break it down, Ono!</i>

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.810
Ono couldn't get past his Lift Upper!

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.180
<i>That's not just a Lift Upper.</i>

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.750
<i>That's his victory pose!</i>

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.250
<i>Yaguchi has evened it up!</i>

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.590
<i>The time has come, Ono.</i>

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.820
<i>The time</i>

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.130
<i>to decide once and for all
which of us is better!</i>

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.530
<i>Haruo! Release everything
you've saved up until now!</i>

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.940
<i>Pour your heart into the Somersault Kick
and your power into the Sonic Boom!</i>

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.440
<i>-Here we go!
-Fight!</i>

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.270
It's round three! This will decide it all!

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.850
<i>Ono, you have no idea
how much I appreciate you.</i>

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:04.020
<i>All I ever needed was games.</i>

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.420
<i>Even when I was made fun of,</i>

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.760
<i>games were my refuge.</i>

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.760
<i>But now, you are my refuge, Ono.</i>

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.140
<i>I love my favorite games even more.</i>

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.640
<i>Thanks to you, I've truly had great fun.</i>

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.080
<i>I can be totally engrossed in</i>

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.750
<i>and totally serious about games
with the one I love.</i>

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.320
<i>That's why I'll fight you now
with all my strength!</i>

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.920
Guile tries to keep his distance
with his Sonic Boom,

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.890
but Zangief won't let him.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.960
It's an intense fight
without either one giving an inch!

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:49.800
Yaguchi's Guile got a Lift Upper in!

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.270
Both endurance gauges are nearly equal!

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.280
He picked him up
while he threw a low kick!

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.980
-Give him a Somersault Kick!
-They're both one blow from losing!

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.220
<i>Jump at me!</i>

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.020
<i>Jump!</i>

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.930
The victor is...

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.870
Akira Ono!

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:48.060
MID-JULY

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.530
Haruo! You're passing it up again today?

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.960
Aren't you going to the arcade?

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:58.830
Today's the release date
for Capcom's new <i>Star Gladiator</i>, right?

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.740
It's Capcom's 3D fighting game, you know.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.040
No, not today.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.410
"Not today either" is more like it.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.080
That's so unlike Haruo.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.410
He's been like that
since he came back from Osaka.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.820
I guess it only makes sense.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.490
He couldn't achieve
what he went there for.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.120
His true intention was to win
and tell her that he loves her.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.330
He had finally come to realize
how he really felt.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:28.300
I wish he were as he always was.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.100
He's much more radiant
when he's a gaming fool.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.600
You're not very radiant lately either.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.140
Have you given up
on those weird hair products?

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.310
What?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.810
I like you the way you are now.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.310
Well, if it isn't Miyao and friends?

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.980
So, what are you boys up to?

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.690
-If you're hitting on chicks, hit on me.
-No.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:53.290
-We're talking about Haruo.
-Haruo?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.430
<i>The "Diet" Screw Piledriver.</i>

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.200
<i>It's a super-high-level technique</i>

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.640
<i>where he whiffs a jumping heavy kick and
uses that motion to avoid my Lift Upper.</i>

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.180
<i>Taking all my Lift Upper punches
in round two</i>

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.010
<i>was in preparation for
the Diet Screw Piledriver.</i>

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:21.450
<i>That was the bait.</i>

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.290
<i>The victor is Akira Ono!</i>

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.560
<i>I didn't know anything,</i>

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:34.030
<i>so I feel like an idiot for waiting until
I beat Ono before telling her how I feel.</i>

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:40.500
<i>Since she lost the championship match,
I know she wasn't there to win it all.</i>

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.240
<i>That's because our fight</i>

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.440
<i>in the semi-final was to be
our last fight.</i>

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:51.750
<i>And I had no idea
what her feelings for me were,</i>

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.380
<i>or that she would move abroad.</i>

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.680
<i>Haruo! Makoto is here!</i>

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.650
Are you disappointed it's me?

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:29.950
What's your problem?

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.450
I bet you feel let-down that it's me
and not my sister that's here.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.790
Quit talking like that.

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.060
Hurry up and come in.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:42.530
You sure sound fine.
I shouldn't have been worried about you.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.500
How unusual. You're reading a manga.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.240
And it doesn't look like
you've been playing any games.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.640
Hey! You really are discouraged,
aren't you?

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:54.510
No, I'm not.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.610
There aren't any games I want to play now.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.050
That's a big fat lie!

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:01.150
It's your nature to complete
those beat 'em up games over and over.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.650
How many times did you complete
<i>Final Fight</i>?

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.550
Eighty-eight times.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.890
That's creepy! You kept count?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:14.000
Akira is leaving...

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:17.270
on the 24th of this month
in the late afternoon.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.070
Make sure you're there to see her off.

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.810
I can't believe how sudden this is.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:28.940
They decide things without considering
their daughter's feelings at all!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:34.480
Will she come back to Japan again
like she did for middle school?

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:38.590
I can't tell you that it won't happen
for sure, Haruo.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.220
But I can say that it won't be easy.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:46.060
You're hurt by this
almost as much as she is.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.530
That's not true.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.500
You're a victim too, Makoto.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:52.070
You'll be separated from your sister.

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:55.740
If anything,
I'm actually the main culprit.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.740
There you go again.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.940
I forced everything on Akira, after all.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:03.780
I'm sorry.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.410
Why are you apologizing, Makoto?

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:08.750
You were just sticking to
your own desires.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.450
What about Akira's desires?

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.860
I'm sure she has her reasons
for what she's doing.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.490
If she agrees with her parents' decision,

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.460
then that's all that matters.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.260
Makoto? Are you crying?

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:22.660
Hey...

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.270
I'm not crying.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:25.670
You aren't?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:30.000
<i>Akira is just showing deference
to our parents and our family.</i>

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:33.670
<i>Even I don't know
what she actually thinks inside.</i>

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.580
But what are your desires, Haruo?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.550
My desires?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:42.520
More importantly, what will you do now?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.120
If you think it's over
because you lost to her,

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.490
won't you regret it
for the rest of your life?

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.930
I almost forgot something important.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.200
Here. This is for you, from Akira.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.430
-What is it? A letter?
-Beats me.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.340
I don't think that's any of my business.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.410
You're not playing games

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.280
and you're not riding
the scooter I gave you.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:12.910
You'll never get over it
if you keep being so wishy-washy.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.650
Now is a turning point
in your life, Haruo.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:22.590
It's time for you to face your feelings
and decide if you'll stick to them.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.630
<i>I sure do talk big.</i>

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.100
<i>Even I don't know what to do.</i>

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.040
<i>I get it now.</i>

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:46.050
<i>The long battle Ono and I fought
for five years is...</i>

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.020
<i>all over now.</i>

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.520
JULY 24

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.500
Haruo, today's the day Akira leaves.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:37.370
Aren't you going to see her off?

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.500
Quit being so wishy-washy!
That's so unlike you!

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.500
If you don't get going now,
you won't make it!

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.370
Tell me why you won't go!

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:49.240
Where do you think you're going?
Are you going to see her?

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:52.350
-No.
-Haruo!

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:53.980
Mom, I'm sorry.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.720
I've thought long and hard,
but I've made up my mind.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.290
I won't see her off.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.220
Wait, Haruo!

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:05.730
NARITA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:20.710
<i>It's just like Mom said.</i>

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:24.510
<i>Why the heck am I being so wishy-washy?</i>

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.010
<i>I'm so lame.</i>

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.020
OUT OF ORDER

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.850
<i>But a loss is a loss.</i>

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:33.650
<i>I was utterly defeated.</i>

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:36.620
Yaguchi.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.130
Hidaka.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.230
It's been a while.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.100
Hidaka, you cut your hair.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:47.070
Yes. Nice and short, right?
It's refreshing. I like it.

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:49.470
What's happened to you, Yaguchi?

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.770
You've got such a grave look.

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:56.040
I guess it's probably about Ono, right?

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.780
Ono is going abroad again, isn't she?

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.650
I heard about it a little while back.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:06.290
For you, this is the second time...

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.220
you'll be apart.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.790
It must be depressing.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.660
Ono sure is important to you.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:18.700
I mean, she's even made
a chatterbox like you silent.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:24.540
Did you know she challenged me
to a match last month?

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:29.140
It was to settle things between us
regarding you, Yaguchi.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:31.150
At least I thought so.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.880
It was a serious battle
between her and me.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:38.320
<i>But I think she actually used the match</i>

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:43.020
<i>to test the strength of
my feelings for you.</i>

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.930
<i>After making up her mind
to go live abroad,</i>

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:48.960
<i>she wanted to surrender you to me.</i>

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:53.370
But Ono was still unsure.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:13:01.280
In our third match, since I was unwilling
to give up my feelings for you,

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.740
she hesitated to put an end to me.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:08.580
In that match, her feelings for you
were painfully clear.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:11.290
Judging from her expression then,

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:15.520
though she had won the match,
she felt she had lost our battle.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:17.290
Once...

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:21.400
Once I understood that,
I had no choice but to back down.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.830
I was just getting in the way.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.370
I know how you went to Osaka together too.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:33.270
<i>Ono conscientiously came to me
for my approval.</i>

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.040
HIDAKA SHOP

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:39.580
I'm sure she wanted to make memories
with you before she left Japan.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.450
Though I had no right to refuse,
she was concerned for me.

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:45.950
It really is touching.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.920
Don't you dare
treat her feelings with disdain.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:55.860
This is where
I fell in love with you, Yaguchi.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:03.800
<i>I was attracted to you because
you were devoted to what you enjoyed.</i>

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.810
That's why I want you to be
devoted to Ono as well.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.010
Hidaka...

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:15.020
I love Ono.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:18.450
I know.

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:23.390
I'm sorry that I completely ignored
your feelings for me.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:26.260
Don't apologize. That just makes it worse.

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:29.260
Hidaka, your advice really hit home.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:33.270
But it's okay. It's all over.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.770
It's laughable, Hidaka.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:40.240
I'm finally paying the price for being
so insensitive to other people's feelings.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.380
Apparently,

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:46.250
what I gave to her in sixth grade was
very precious to her.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.320
The other day,
she returned it via her sister.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:52.620
Later this afternoon, she's leaving Japan.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.420
She's through with me now.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.230
-What was it?
-What?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:01.330
What did she return to you?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.760
It's nothing special.

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:06.070
It's a cheap kid's ring
I got at an arcade.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.970
You idiot! It's already late afternoon!

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.910
What the heck are you doing here?
She's leaving today!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.810
It's so unlike you
to wallow in sentimentality!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:21.520
A ring? You're so stupid! Did you think
it was over because she gave it back?

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:23.750
Is that why you were acting so hurt?

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:27.960
I knew it! You have absolutely
no idea what Ono's feelings are!

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:29.960
Her feelings are the exact opposite!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.960
She's telling you she wants you
to bring that when you see her off!

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:34.930
Go, Yaguchi!

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:39.130
Living your life true to your desires is
the best way to live!

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.870
That's what you told me yourself!

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.100
I'm sure Ono is waiting for you, Yaguchi!

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.270
Hurry, Yaguchi!

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.310
HIDAKA SHOP

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.140
Mom!

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:51.440
Mom?

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:53.810
You've made up your mind, I see!

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:56.180
You're still my son!

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:58.680
Ride! With all the speed you can muster!

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:01.080
Show them you're a man!

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:11.690
<i>The Den-en-toshi Line is running
behind schedule due to signal trouble.</i>

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.660
<i>I'll never be able to
live down this regret.</i>

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:20.400
<i>All I focused on was what I liked,
so I missed what was important.</i>

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.170
<i>I'm hopeless.</i>

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.170
<i>I'm a hopeless idiot!</i>

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.140
<i>How did I become so stubborn?</i>

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:31.150
<i>Why did I decide it was all over?</i>

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:35.120
<i>After all those times I lost to Ono,</i>

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:38.590
<i>I never once admitted
it was all over and gave up!</i>

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.090
<i>Why did I put an end to our competition?</i>

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:49.030
<i>My fear of facing the woman I love
turned me into a coward.</i>

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.370
<i>I was a wimp when facing
what I could do nothing about.</i>

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.940
<i>I'm a worthless loser,
too much of a wussy to go after her.</i>

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:59.040
<i>Realizing it now is too late!
I won't make it.</i>

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:00.610
<i>There's no way I'll make it!</i>

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:03.380
<i>It was over when the trains stopped.</i>

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.080
<i>It'll take forever to get to
the airport by scooter!</i>

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:09.480
<i>There will also be traffic
in the late afternoon.</i>

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:13.350
I won't make it! Ono's already gone!

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:17.220
Ono has left Japan!

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:33.210
What's going on? My car won't move!

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:34.310
<i>Did it break down?</i>

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.820
<i>Haruo!</i>

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:44.220
<i>Lay down a barrage of Sonic Booms
and blast ahead!</i>

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:49.090
<i>Don't give up!</i>

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:51.290
<i>You have to go, even if you're late!</i>

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.230
<i>Straight ahead at full power!</i>

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:56.530
<i>Just like how you've always played games!</i>

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:01.300
<i>Face this battle
with pride and conviction!</i>

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:06.070
<i>That's right! She's gotten ahead of me
time and time again!</i>

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.980
<i>So I sure as heck won't let up now!</i>

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:21.050
I want to see Ono!

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.460
I want to see her right now!

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:26.260
Ono!

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.710
<i>Love makes it possible.</i>

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:43.680
<i>Love makes it a reality!</i>

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.980
<i>For all the love you've given us,</i>

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:48.450
<i>let us repay you now!</i>

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:57.260
<i>Sonic Boom!</i>

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:05.500
NARITA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.410
Where the hell have you been?

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:17.340
You're all scratched up!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.680
Who cares?

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:20.510
Has Ono left?

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:21.980
She's gone!

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:25.390
She's gone, but the plane is
turning around and coming back!

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:29.320
There's turbulence
or some kind of technical problem.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.370
Ono!

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:44.240
I won't let you win and run off!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:45.740
I won't stand for it!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.370
Our competition isn't over yet!

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:52.010
It's our fate to keep competing,
so there's no way I'll let it end!

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:54.310
Even if you go abroad,
I won't let you get away.

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:56.880
I'll get a passport and go see you.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:21:00.750
Don't cry!
It's my turn to cry at the airport!

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.530
Ono...

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:10.330
I love you.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.630
I love you so much, it drives me wild!

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:16.370
I'm sure I'll keep losing to you,

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:18.310
but I don't care.

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:22.310
I want to keep challenging you!
I want to live in constant competition!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.480
I always want to be near you!

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:28.420
To make you my wife,
I swear I'll come for you.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.620
Will you accept this?

00:21:57.480 --> 00:22:00.380
<i>Haruo, this isn't the end.</i>

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:03.420
<i>You've merely cleared a single stage.</i>

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:07.390
<i>We'll keep fighting
to give you the best possible ending.</i>

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.060
<i>It's the same with you too.</i>

00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:16.430
<i>This battle will give you both new power!</i>

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:24.070
ORIGINAL WORK BY RENSUKE OSHIKIRI
